after loki episode 4 the nexus event  ended with a shocking cliffhanger the  way for episode 5 was excruciating but  now the latest installment journey into  mystery has arrived and with it some big  questions  here's the ending of loki episode 5  explained  it's established very quickly thanks to  a forced confession from judge renslayer  to sylvie that the tva's pruning batons  don't actually kill variants instead  they transport them to a place in time  called the void where they can be  vaporized by a malevolent smoky force  called goliath  the void's existence is obviously a  highly classified tba secret which is  why loki didn't learn about it when he  was asking for files from the clerk back  in episode 2.  in marvel comics goliath is closely tied  to a notorious time traveling villain  who many fans are expecting to see very  soon in ant-man and the wasp quantomania  kang the conqueror  and he's reportedly being played by  lovecraft country star jonathan magers  the big smokey beast had his own  temporal empire when he was originally  introduced back in 1993's avengers  determinatrix objective number one  but kang constructed a time barrier to  keep the villain out of his own domain  called chronopolis  that doesn't sound too dissimilar to  what the tva has done with eliath and  loki trapping the entity in the void so  they can use him to wipe out pesky  variants and other things that don't  belong in the sacred timeline  the bulk of the episode follows our main  loki chatting with the other variants  and discovering what makes him so  different from himself  all while trying to find a way to defeat  goliath and figure out who's really  behind the tva  the episode doesn't rush through things  giving this god squad plenty of time to  bounce off one another all while  expanding the mythology and development  of everyone's favorite god of mischief  classic loki explains how he lived past  the events of avengers infinity war  he reveals that he conjured an illusion  of himself so exacting that he fooled  thanos into thinking that decoy was real  and that he killed loki from there  classic loki went into hiding as  inanimate debris  cowardly and smart yes that's classic  loki alright  but not only is it an insightful  anecdote as to what loki's are capable  of when they put their mind to it  it's also a clue as to how the vibrantly  dressed character will have an impact in  the final fight against elia  it all ends in a big scuffle when a  variant will call president loki shows  up with an army of other variant loki's  from across the void's wasteland  however they all start betraying each  other because that's just what loki's do  isn't it at this point it looks like the  small appearance from president loki  might debunk a few of those theories  suggesting that he's the one behind the  tva  it's still not impossible but it's  highly unlikely  they just couldn't stay apart for too  long could they silvi follows loki to  the void after renslayer reveals that  the void is a place at the end of the  timeline  that means it's out of harm's way and  can't affect past events  sylvie's self-pruning shows that the  variant clearly cares as deeply for the  main loki as he cares for her her main  motivation is finding out who's really  behind the tva  but she's just not very good at  expressing her emotions  this is something that comes across very  clearly in a touching moment leading up  to the final battle  while kid classic and gator loki shelter  in a hollowed-out building with mobius  loki and sylvie huddled together in a  conjured blanket while they try to  untangle the romantic mess they created  for themselves  it's clearly the first time sylvie has  ever let herself be vulnerable with  anyone so it's quite fitting that she's  opening up to an alternate version of  herself  but she even struggles to connect with  loki i don't have  friends  i don't have anyone  finally loki gets his own redemption arc  because he promises not to betray sylvie  he hugs mobius and calls him a friend  before the tva agent heads  back to work to burn it down loki and  silvi head off to face a liat themselves  while the rest of the god squad decides  to stay in the void  after all this is their home now  thankfully sylvie vetoes loki's simple  plan of trying to stab a smoke monster  and goes with her idea of enchanting the  creature and revealing where and who the  person behind the tba is  however just because she's been  nefariously murderous up to this point  doesn't mean she can't inspire loki to  have a little faith in himself  he unlocks his own enchanting abilities  just in the nick of time on the  battlefield with a little  encouragement from sylvie thankfully  classic loki decides to give his life  glorious purpose by creating a fake  asgard to distract elia  it's a brilliant moment to witness  especially for an older bitter version  of the character to finally feel like  he's doing something positive in the  timeline rather than constantly being a  villain  his trickery succeeds but at the cost of  his life however classic loki points out  earlier on that he cheated death by  conjuring a fake version of himself  during the confrontation with thanos so  who knows  once eliath is enchanted the smoke  clears to show a bizarre castle or manor  in the middle of a swirling cosmic  background  with all the kang the conqueror  connections to eliyah is it possible  that this is chronopolis  goliath clearly couldn't get inside it  in the comics chronopolis lies on the  outskirts of limbo and contains time  points to places under kang's control  will we see jonathan majors as kang next  week in the loki finale  only time will tell check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about loki are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

